    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d107">

                <pb facs="0309" n="289" xml:id="pg289"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 767.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-25"><hi rendition="#italic">August
                                25,</hi> 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> A telegram was received at this legation
                    yesterday, at one o’clock p. m., from the consular agent at Dover, announcing
                    the arrival of the steamer Niagara, on her way to Antwerp. The Georgia had been
                    taken and sent as prize to the United States. The crew were landed at Dover.</p>
                <p>This event has made some sensation here. The newspapers express opinions based on
                    little information, and prompted by their respective predilections in our
                    struggle. Should any official indication be made visible in the Times to-morrow
                    morning I shall send a copy with the despatch.</p>
                <p>I am your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
